  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "With only two completed experiments, evidence is sparse. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieved 48.5% acc, while config_010 (image_only, resnet50) was poor at 20.8%. The most fundamental uncertainty is whether the RNA representation itself is the bottleneck: does a learned encoder (scvi_n200) meaningfully outperform a linear one (pca_n2000)? config_004 changes only the RNA encoder from config_001, providing a clean single-variable comparison. If scvi_n200 substantially improves accuracy, it signals that representation quality is a key lever and justifies investing in learned encoders for all downstream (multiprofile, multimodal) experiments. If it does not, we know the representation is not the limiting factor and should prioritize testing profile setting, aggregation, or modality fusion instead. This is the highest-information next step under a tight budget because it isolates one critical design axis before committing to more complex configurations."
}

